{"id": "EUVD-2026-103954", "enisaUuid": "536fc5fc-1c53-3738-9c67-f8fb25b813e5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211: set info->band for 802.3 encap offload frames\n\nUnlike the 802.11 TX paths, ieee80211_8023_xmit() does not set\ninfo->band from the channel context on non-MLD interfaces. It stays at\n0, so ieee80211_get_tx_rates() uses the wrong band for these frames.\n\nSet it the same way as ieee80211_build_hdr(): drop the frame if there is\nno channel context, and leave the band at 0 on MLD interfaces.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:46:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:49", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6535f7084d95873785a7a93cdca05e8ee83b5601", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/93c1b247224a32f546b616a8fe87b9bab20f0a7f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9cedbfde1450028f530e9af950f53491fcaebfeb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d9c5525bbc1a548cdc9c4def3cd7fbfc7c66b5b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4febc02cd02f021f2b6d0768332be643ef14a12d"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5cc8-qw42-jp7f", "CVE-2026-98700"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a35fc79-059d-38cd-bb3c-43f17be3f08b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "50ff477a8639fa1fbbeecb5a6f2f8b6c5557ecec <9cedbfde1450028f530e9af950f53491fcaebfeb"}, {"id": "1a67842e-af21-3782-ad33-075cbeb53d00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "30882c0d-1fe5-3f87-9d73-84ae2300d53f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "3d444e6a-c755-3601-97d8-856043c187c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "732cdeac-0c9c-3609-91c8-9b49c32ea280", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.7"}, {"id": "899fb8bf-2b3f-37dd-86fc-ceba1b92a823", "pro